    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 all 17 tests pass, including the new `Cp09Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment for `POST /api/owners`, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\nThe change follows the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n1. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode.java` (`rest/function/owner/`): reads the built `Owner` via `@Val`, computes `LAST3` (upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`, safely handling short names) and `NNNN` = `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` zero-padded to 4 digits, then sets it on the entity in place.\n\n2. **Wiring** \u2014 inserted `assignCustomerCode` into `owners.POST.yml` between `defaultRegistrationDate` and `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`. Running before `save` means the count excludes the not-yet-persisted new owner, so each owner gets the next global sequence \u2014 exactly \"one more than the current number of owners.\"\n\n3. **Entity** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter to `Owner`.\n\n4. **Persistence** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, postgres, mysql).\n\n5. **Response DTO** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` (the generated `OwnerDto`), so MapStruct maps it by name; added `@Mapping(target = \"customerCode\", ignore = true)` to the `OwnerFieldsDto \u2192 Owner` mapping since the request body carries no code.\n\nThe `Cp09Tests` assertions pass: `smithers \u2192 SMI-...`, `jones \u2192 JON-...`, and the two codes' sequence numbers differ by exactly 1.",
